     "body": "### What I run\n\nTwo Claude Desktop profiles from the same signed build, on Windows:\n\n- **vanilla** — its own userData dir, launched with `--user-data-dir=%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Claude-1p` and `CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR=1`\n- **magpie** — the default profile `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Claude-3p`, connected to magpie's gateway\n\nBoth are the same `Claude.exe`. Only the userData dir differs.\n\n### What magpie does today\n\nThe Agents tab lists a single `Claude Desktop` row. Internally:\n\n- `sessionResolver.roots` is `[.../Claude, .../Claude-3p]` — used to attribute a call to an account, not to list anything\n- 3p calls are folded into the one agent (`sessions.Call{Agent: \"claude-desktop\", Session: \"third-3p\"}`)\n- `internal/profile` is a settings snapshot (`Snapshot`/`Save`/`Apply`), not a second install\n\nSo a second profile is invisible, and the model/effort picked in that single row applies to whichever profile magpie wrote into.\n\n### What I'd like\n\n1. **Discover desktop profiles** — the default roots (`Claude`, `Claude-3p`) plus any extra root the user names. The app already accepts `CLAUDE_USER_DATA_DIR=1` with `--user-data-dir=<dir>` as an escape hatch for running a second profile.\n2. **One agent row per profile** — e.g. `claude-desktop` and `claude-desktop@<profile>`, each with its own model / effort / subagent squares.\n3. **Keep today's single-row behaviour** when only one profile exists, so nothing changes for people who never split them.\n\n### Notes\n\n- The CLI already tells the two apart: `CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT` is `claude-desktop` for 1p and `claude-desktop-3p` for 3p. Only the listing collapses them.\n- My install has a `claude-desktop.profile` stash key that nothing ever writes — maybe that was the intended place.\n- Related: #2705, #3117, #4333.\n\n### Why it matters here\n\nI keep one profile on magpie (models from my gateway) and one vanilla profile signed into Anthropic, and I need different model routing on each. Right now the vanilla profile can't be reached from magpie at all.\n",
